imple graph once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/joined(by:)-3vukc":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/joined(by:)-3vukc","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/joined(by:)-3vukc","abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"joined"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"by"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"prec